          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>Monomers basically create blocks for molecules, including proteins, starch and many other polymers. Four big monomers are found:&nbsp;amino acids, nucleotides, monosaccharides, and fatty acids. The main forms of macromolecules are those monomers: proteins, nucleic acids, carbohydrates, and lipids.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/015f7191-e2a9-424a-a21d-fd08f73c0e95-6ad25077-1d9a-4f17-abbe-482d256b3f5d-9e325498-0795-41b0-acba-97fdccd22eef-image.png\" style=\"width: 537px; height: 436px;\" /></p>",
